to getting your PhD at the time. So what led you to think I would be better at that than at being a scientist, a job that also involves looking stuff up a lot? Well, I think to be a scientist, and I didn't know this because I was very good at study in science, but I didn't really have the experience of being an actual scientist. And there's a real difference in the type of, I don't, it's like ego, but I don't mean that in any pejorative sense that you're driven by the thing you want to discover so much,
